            title: "Purpose and Clinical Indication",
            content: "The Timed Up and Go (TUG) test is a simple and widely used clinical tool to assess a person's mobility, balance, and risk of falling. It is particularly useful in elderly populations and individuals with neurological conditions that affect balance and gait, such as stroke.",
