            content: "• Assistive Devices: Patients should use their regular walking aid (cane, walker) if needed, and this should be documented.\\n• Safety: The examiner should stand by to provide assistance if the patient loses their balance.\\n• Simplicity: The TUG's simplicity, minimal equipment requirement, and quick administration time make it an excellent screening tool in various clinical settings.",
